    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, why would we offer a lower-value item? That feels like it complicates things. If the sensor logs are so clear that the package was handled correctly, wouldn't the most \"efficient\" move be to deny the claim entirely to save the cost? I'm trying to understand if you're recommending we pay out just to avoid the hassle, even when the data suggests we shouldn't have to.",
