      "content": "While denying the claim is the most cost-efficient route based purely on the logs, it carries a very high risk of escalating the conflict and losing the customer entirely. Even if the claim is technically unfounded, absorbing a small cost now is cheaper than the long-term cost of negative reviews and lost future business. A fixed, firm resolution, like a partial refund, prevents the claim from spiraling into a more protracted and expensive dispute.",
